OK current reqs for this are defined in 2.0 as 

```py
    @property
    def has_temp_table(self):
        """target dialect supports checking a single temp table name

        unfortunately this is not the same as temp_table_names

        """

        return only_on(["sqlite", "oracle", "postgresql", "mssql"]) + skip_if(
            self._sqlite_file_db
        )


```

why not sqlite file?   for Mysql /mariadb we'd have to use DESCRIBE and just use the cursor directly to avoid the whole error handling cycle
